 ('Write a 6-sentence biographical paragraph about a public speaker you admire, using a relative clause, an appositive and all the more.','Wangari Maathai, a Kenyan environmentalist and Nobel laureate, founded the Green Belt Movement in 1977. She taught rural women to plant trees, an act that linked ecology to dignity. Her speeches, which were plain and patient, made her demands all the more persuasive. She is widely regarded as a pioneer of community-led conservation. She kept campaigning despite arrests and threats. Her legacy lives in millions of trees.',['Usei **aposto**','Usei **oração relativa**','Usei **all the more**'],'6 frases'),
