 ('Reading · An editorial',text('Editorial: Disagree Better',['Public debate is rarely short of passion; it is **short of patience**. **Granted**, anger has driven reforms, and **no one should be asked** to be polite about injustice. **Yet** a culture in which every opponent is **a villain** leaves no room for compromise, **let alone** trust.','We **urge** public figures to **argue the point, not the person**; to **quote opponents fairly**; and to **concede** what is true in the other side’s case. **Civility is not weakness**: it is **the condition under which arguments can be won**. **Were** more of us to practise it, our disagreements **would be fiercer in substance and calmer in tone**.'],kicker='EDITORIAL',by='The Editorial Board',gloss=[('concede','conceder'),('villain','vilão'),('fierce','intenso'),('compromise','acordo, concessão')])),
 [('The editorial says anger has never helped reforms.','F','Granted, anger has driven reforms.'),('It urges leaders to quote opponents fairly.','T','quote opponents fairly.'),('It claims civility is a weakness.','F','Civility is not weakness.')],
 [('“Granted” (no início de frase) = ?',['É verdade que (concessão)','Concedido oficialmente','Garantido'],0,'Granted, ... = concordo que, mas...'),('“let alone” = ?',['muito menos','deixar sozinho','deixe-se só'],0,'let alone = e muito menos.')],
